.. raw:: html

    <div class="sphx-glr-thumbcontainer" tooltip="Euclid&#x27;s Elements (Book VII, Propositions 1-2) finds the greatest common divisor by repeating \gcd(a, b) = \gcd(b, a \bmod b) until the remainder vanishes. This script traces the division steps for one pair, recovers Bézout&#x27;s coefficients ax + by = \gcd(a, b) with extended_gcd, and maps how many steps the algorithm needs: the slowest inputs are consecutive Fibonacci numbers (Lamé, 1844).">

